This API allows you to manage your Managed Databases for MongoDB®.

USAGE:
  scw mongodb <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  database    Database management commands
  endpoint    Endpoint management commands
  instance    Instance management commands
  maintenance Maintenance management commands
  node-type   Node types management commands
  snapshot    Snapshot management commands
  user        User management commands
  version     MongoDB® major version management commands

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for mongodb
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw mongodb [command] --help" for more information about a command.
